\newlabel{sec:synthk}{{3.4}{9}{RQ4: Controlled multiplicity: the inversion switches on at \texorpdfstring {$k{=}2$}{k=2}, ramps further only for the strongest judges, and the obvious fixes underperform}{subsection.3.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Takeaway: for the two judges shown the reference helps at $k{=}1$ and inflates at high $k$, the any-correct-answer instruction closes phi-4's gap but not Qwen-7B's, and multiple references reduce Qwen-7B's $k{=}16$ gap without matching blind (overlapping intervals).} Excess hack gap (baseline SD) per multiplicity stratum on the synthetic Qwen-generator pool, for the Qwen2.5-7B and phi-4 judges under four context conditions. Point estimates are descriptive; the inferential claims are the paired contrasts in the text (\texttt  {synthk\_paired.json}). Values rounded from \texttt  {synthk\_results.json}; per-stratum bootstrap CIs are quoted in the text. The Qwen-7B rows are a generator-equals-judge cell on this pool.}}{10}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:synthk}{{2}{10}{\textbf {Takeaway: for the two judges shown the reference helps at $k{=}1$ and inflates at high $k$, the any-correct-answer instruction closes phi-4's gap but not Qwen-7B's, and multiple references reduce Qwen-7B's $k{=}16$ gap without matching blind (overlapping intervals).} Excess hack gap (baseline SD) per multiplicity stratum on the synthetic Qwen-generator pool, for the Qwen2.5-7B and phi-4 judges under four context conditions. Point estimates are descriptive; the inferential claims are the paired contrasts in the text (\texttt {synthk\_paired.json}). Values rounded from \texttt {synthk\_results.json}; per-stratum bootstrap CIs are quoted in the text. The Qwen-7B rows are a generator-equals-judge cell on this pool}{table.caption.9}{}}
